, but clearly they are not now, since {le} as {zo'e voi} is exactly paralle=
l to {lo} as {zo'e noi} (I would have thought {poi}, but then I don't know =
what {zo'e} means, anyhow).
If you mean by "'can' and 'any' are related" that the the modal context of =
"can" is one of the places where "any" is an appropriate (even more clear) =
way "some" (or, from a different point of view, "all"), then you are right,=
 but the rules about "any" are basically the same regardless of which conte=
xt is involved, modal or negative or ... . I suspect you just not yet comfo=
rtable with using these rules in Lojban.




